<title>USA: St Paul hogs up $2.00-2.50 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Paul hogs up $2.00-2.50 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST PAUL 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said barrows and gilts compared with Tuesday, were slow, prices were $2.00 to mostly $2.50 higher. Top $53.00 per cwt.</p>
<p>    US 1-3	  220-250 lbs    53.00, few 52.50</p>
<p>			250-260 lbs    52.50-53.00</p>
<p>			260-270 lbs    51.50-52.50</p>
<p>    US 2-3	  270-280 lbs    50.50-51.50</p>
<p>Sows - up $1.00/off $1.00. Top $49.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-3	   300-450 lbs    42.50</p>
<p>			 450-500 lbs    46.00</p>
<p>			 500-550 lbs    47.00, few 48.00</p>
<p>			 550-700 lbs    49.00</p>
</text>
